  "body": "The parent #4233 is merged (`7cb5da575`); this PR now shows only its own commits.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds eight MCP tools for tool components, tool assemblies and the user component library. The tools are in three new files of `crates/app/src/mcp/`: `component_tools.rs`, `assembly_tools.rs` and `component_library_tools.rs`.\n\nRead tools:\n- `list_tool_components`: lists the built-in components, the user library and the document component table. The filters are `kind`, `scope` and `compatible_with`. A row of a match has `fits: [{as, port}]`. A document row has its library sync status.\n- `get_tool_assembly`: gives the component stack of a document tool. It gives each node with its mount (parent, port, Z rotation, stickout `projection_mm`), its MCS frame and its sync status. It also gives the derived cutting diameter and corner radius, the gauge length, and the `links` input form.\n\nDocument write tools. Each tool runs the same undoable command as the GUI, in one History step:\n- `upsert_tool_component` (`UpsertDocumentComponent`)\n- `delete_tool_component` (`DeleteDocumentComponent`)\n- `set_tool_assembly` (`SetToolAssembly`; `links: null` clears the stack)\n- `sync_tool_component` (`SyncDocumentComponent`)\n\nUser library tools. These are file edits through `component_library::store`, not undoable commands:\n- `save_library_component`\n- `delete_library_component`\n\nEach tool validates its arguments early and refuses by name. A component goes through the MCP door in the `.camproj` wire form (`ComponentDto`, `deny_unknown_fields`). A stack goes through as `LinkDto`. A stated `library_ref` in an upsert or a save is refused. A `builtin:` id is refused for a library save and delete. An optional `library` argument names another `.camcomponents` file, as the cut recipe tools do.\n\nLive GUI gate (`mcp/live.rs`): the two library write tools are `FileWrite`. A stated `library` on `list_tool_components`, `get_tool_assembly` and `sync_tool_component` is `FilePathAccess`.\n\nThe `camcraft-mcp` skill lists each new tool (section 4). This is a process file, so the body has the line `Process change: yes`. The PR does not change `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3647-component-mcp-tools.md`.\n\nDocs: the generated tool reference `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and the user guide `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md` list the new tools. The `mcp_doc_drift` suite pins both.\n\nNo script verb: the skill does not ask for one, and the script host has no component verbs.\n\n## Readings and pinning tests\n\nNew submodule `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/component_mcp.rs` in the existing `tool_library_holders` suite (no new test binary). All calls go through the MCP server:\n- `component_mcp::mcp_lists_compatible_components_and_reads_a_built_assembly`: `compatible_with` the shared insert gives the two cutter bodies, with `{as: parent, port: CSW1}`. An assembly built by `set_tool_assembly` reads back Ø25, corner radius 0.4, three nodes. Undo, redo and clear work.\n- `component_mcp::mcp_edits_a_shared_insert_and_syncs_it_from_the_library`: one upsert of the shared insert updates both tools (corner radius 0.4 to 0.8) in one undo step. A save and a link-only sync, then a newer library copy shows `update_available`. The sync updates both tools, and undo and redo work. A library delete shows `missing_from_library`.\n- `component_mcp::mcp_component_tools_refuse_by_name_and_change_nothing`: about twenty named refusals (an incompatible insert, an unknown key, `library_ref`, a no-op, a used component, unknown ids, a bad link key, an empty stack, an insert on a coupling port, unknown kind or scope or argument, `builtin:` ids, id and component together). No refused save writes the library file, and the assembly does not change.\n\n## Gate results (head `dda741331`)\n\nThe gate base is `qsmits/issue/3645-component-library` (the #4233 head `745234df7`), not `main`. This PR stacks on that branch.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_library_holders`: 28 passed, 0 failed (3 new tests).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_doc_drift`: 9 passed. The first quick run found that the generated reference `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and the guide `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md` did not list the new tools. The second commit adds them.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base qsmits/issue/3645-component-library`: 169 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (28.3 min, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`). Two earlier runs stopped at the build with `can't find crate for solidcore` (a stale `solidcore` unit in the target folder, not this change); `cargo clean -p solidcore -p solidcore-convert` cleared it.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed (15.9 min).\n- No heavy step (P6).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A live GUI session (`--mcp-port`) with the approval prompts. Only the classification in `requires_approval` changed.\n- The default user library folder. The tests use the `library` argument, so they do not write the user's real library.\n- A lathe-held assembly. The resolver refuses it by name (#3643).\n\n## Notes\n\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders.rs` goes from 407 to 411 lines: two lines for the module and two lines for the header and Gate map. The test code is in the submodule.\n- `mcp/tools.rs` gets one line (`component_tools::all()`). It was already over 400 lines.\n\nChangelog: MCP tools for tool components and assemblies: list_tool_components (with compatible_with), get_tool_assembly, upsert_tool_component, delete_tool_component, set_tool_assembly, sync_tool_component, save_library_component and delete_library_component.\n\nEffort: medium (not escalated)\n\nFixes #3647\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
